# Single source of truth

When two surfaces answer the same question (what is a Looker token, which methods move a token, how a clock is computed), reuse the existing function or catalog. Do not copy ids, labels, or branching into a second list.

- Derive, don't duplicate. A consumer may add a local exclusion (example: event log skips postMessage / iframe navigation) but must not restate the shared identity rule.
- Prefer `tokenLaneId`, `docs/token-method-map.json`, and server snapshot fields over hardcoded token-id sets.
- If a new copy appears, delete it and call the original. Keep the tree lean.
